< basic.at {for all, etc.}
< parameters.at {for dual_inner_class}

{dualQ.at

  dualQ@Param, the Vogan duality map, built as the mirror image of endo@Param in
  endo_claude.at; and Q_row@Param, which computes a row of the Q polynomial matrix
  of G as a single ordinary KL column on the dual side, from a PARTIAL block.

  THE SYMMETRY.  Both endo and dualQ anchored at the bottom of a
  regular block, where down_move runs out. endo works up from there
  both in G and in the endoscopic group E. dualQ works up in G and
  down in the dual group dG (from the top of the dual block). The
  bottom of the block (in G or E) has a single KGBElt and several
  lambdas. The top of any regular block (like the dual block in dG)
  has one lambda and several KGBElts with the same involution.

    in endo, endox(q) is computable from q.x alone, so x is known at every step and
       the walk supplies lambda.  The search at the anchor is over shifts, which move
       lambda.  The two valued Cayley is two valued in x, resolved against endox.

    in dualQ, dlambda(q) = dgamma - torus_factor(q.x) is computable from q.x alone,
       so lambda is known at every step and the walk supplies dx.  The search at the
       anchor is over torus factor corrections, which move dx.  The two valued Cayley
       is two valued in lambda, resolved by taking the known dlambda.

  THREE THINGS THAT HAD TO BE RIGHT.

    1. The anchor is the split end, not the compact end.  At the compact end lambda is
       constant, so dlambda carries no information and distinct parameters collapse to
       the same dual.

    2. The torus factor correction must be allowed to be HALF integral.

    3. The validity test for a torus factor is the kernel's, not the script's.  Every
       simple root of the inner class must take an EVEN value on tf*(1+theta); see
       atlas-types.w.  square_is_central in parameters.at is weaker and admits torus
       factors that then abort with "Torus factor does not define a valid strong
       involution".

  The dual infinitesimal character is bgv + k*rho(dGi) with k the smallest ODD k
  making it regular dominant.  k must be odd so that (k-1)*rho stays in X^*.
  In every group tested the smallest odd regular k is 1 or 3.

  WHAT IS VERIFIED.  Over SL(3,R), SL(4,R), SU(2,1), SU(2,2), SU(3,2), Sp(6,R),
  Sp(8,R), SO(4,3), SO(5,4), Spin(4,3), Spin(6,1), Spin(5,2), Spin(7,2), Spin(6,2),
  G2_s and F4_s, at every dominant gamma built from fundamental weights with
  denominators up to 2, including singular gamma:

    - sig is injective into a single dual block, and Q[i][j] = P[sig[j]][sig[i]];
    - Q_row(p) agrees with row p of KL_Q_polynomials of the block, with no nonzero
      entry falling outside the partial block.

  The five SU(3,2) infinitesimal characters where dualB alone lands in the split dual
  real form instead of sl(2,H).gl(1,R) are included, and need no special case: the
  correction search finds the half integral torus factor by itself.

}

{ ------------------------------------------------------- torus factor validity }

{ the library's own test, from atlas-types.w }
set tf_is_valid (InnerClass ic, mat theta, ratvec tf) = bool:
   let v = ratvec: tf*(1+theta) in
   all(for a in ic.simple_roots do is_integer((v*a)/2) od)

{ ------------------------------------------------------------- the block walk }

{ index of an integral simple root that is C+ (x status 4) or noncompact imaginary
  (x status 3); -1 when there is none, i.e. when q is at the bottom of its block
  (most split) }
set down_move (Param q) = int:
(  let id = integrality_datum(q), x = q.x
in first(for a@j in id.simple_roots do status(a,q.x)>= 3 od)
)

set at_bottom_reg (Param q) = bool: down_move(q) < 0 and is_regular(q)

{ index of an integral simple root that is C- (status 0) or real parity
  (status 2 or 3); -1 at the top of the block, which is where both maps anchor }
set up_move (Param q) = int:
(  let id = integrality_datum(q), x = q.x
in first(for a@j in id.simple_roots do let stat = status(a,q) in stat < 4 and stat != 1 od)
)

set at_top_reg (Param q) = bool: up_move(q) < 0 and is_regular(q)

{ ------------------------------------------- the crude dual, and the correction }

{ dualB's dual inner class, dual involution and uncorrected torus factor }
set dual_crude (Param p) = (InnerClass,mat,ratvec):
   (dual_inner_class(p), -(p.x.involution).^, p.infinitesimal_character - p.lambda)

{ half integral corrections inside the +1 eigenlattice of the dual involution }
set dual_steps (mat dtheta) = [ratvec]:
   let M = eigen_lattice(dtheta,1) in for b in box(4,#M) do ratvec: (M*b)/2 od

{ the corrections admissible at q: valid torus factor, and the right grading, so
  that a real integral coroot of q is parity exactly when it is noncompact on the
  dual side }
set dual_corrections (Param q) = [ratvec]:
(  let (dGi,dtheta,dtf) = dual_crude(q), theta = q.x.involution
   then id = integrality_datum(q)
   then reals = for av in id.poscoroots if av*(theta+1) = null(#av) do av fi od
   then want = for av in reals do parity(q,av) od
   then good = [ratvec]:[]
in for s in dual_steps(dtheta)
   do if tf_is_valid(dGi,dtheta,dtf+s)
      then let dx = KGB_elt(dGi,dtheta,dtf+s) then ok = true in
         for av@i in reals do if (status(av,dx)=3) != want[i] then ok:=false fi od
      ;  if ok then good := good##[s] fi
      fi
   od
;  good
)

{ ------------------------------------------------------------- the dual KGB elt }

set undual_hash = make_Param_hash()
set dual_list = [Param]:[]

{
regular infinitesimal character NOT assumed; but see also dualQ below for the
  general case.  Walking down in G (toward split; includes nc imag
  Cayley) is walking up in the dual (toward discrete series; include
  real parity Cayley), so the dual Cayley is single valued on KGB
  elements and the lambda ambiguity is settled by dlambda.
}
set dual = (Param->Param):
  rec_fun my_dual (Param q) Param:
  ( let n = undual_hash.lookup(q)
    in if n < 0
       then let ans = let j = down_move(q), dg = ratvec: []
       	    then dGi = dual_inner_class(q)
   	    then bgv = base_grading_vector(q.real_form), tf = q.x.torus_factor
   	    then rdv = dGi.root_datum, drho = rho(dGi)
   	    then dom_reg_flag = false, m = -1
	    then () = while not dom_reg_flag
   		      do m+:=1;
			dg := bgv + (2*m+1)*drho;
		        dom_reg_flag := all(for av in rdv.poscoroots do av*dg > 0 od)
		      od {now dg is dominant regular}
       	    	  in if j<0 {q is most split}
     	       	     then let (dGi,dtheta,dtf) = dual_crude(q)
               	    	  then sols = dual_corrections(q)
               	    	  then s = ratvec:
	       	    	       if #sols=0
	       	    	       then prints("no dual_x found at ",q);
	       	    	       	    null(#dtf)
 	       	    	       else sols[0]
	       	    	       fi
       	            	  then d_x = KGB_elt(dGi,dtheta,dtf+s)
		    	  in parameter(d_x,dg-q.x.torus_factor,dg)
     	       	     else let id = integrality_datum(q) {case j>= 0}
       	       	     	  then a = vec: id.simple_roots[j], av = vec: id.simple_coroots[j]
       		    	  in if status(a,q.x)=4
          	       	     then cross(av, my_dual(cross(a,q)))
          	       	     else let guess = Cayley(av, my_dual(Cayley(a,q)))
		       	       	  in parameter(guess.x, dg-tf, dg)
		       	    {down, so  inner is nc imag Cayley, landing at real
	       		     parity; outer has av imag nc, so dual Cayley on KGB is
			     single-valued.}
          	       	     fi
	       	     fi {now ans is the right answer}
		 in let N = undual_hash.size()
		    in n := undual_hash.match(q);
		       if n=N
		       then dual_list#:=ans
		       fi
      fi;
      dual_list[n]
  )

{ -------------------------------------------------------------- the dual itself }

{
{ x, lambda and nu of the dual, with the smallest odd regular dominant multiplier }
set dual_pieces (Param p) = (KGBElt,ratvec,ratvec):
(  let x = dual_x(p), dGi = dual_inner_class(p)
   then bgv = base_grading_vector(p.real_form), tf = p.x.torus_factor
   then rdv = dGi.root_datum, drho = ratvec: rho(dGi)
   then dom_reg_flag = false, k = -1, dg = ratvec:[]
in while not dom_reg_flag
   do k+:=1;
      dg := bgv + (2*k+1)*drho;
      dom_reg_flag:= all(for av in rdv.poscoroots do av*dg > 0 od)
   od
;  let dg = ratvec: bgv + k*drho in (x, dg-tf, dg)
)

set dual_reg (Param p) = Param:
   assert(@:is_regular(p));
   let (dx,dlam,dnu) = dual_pieces(p)
   in parameter(dx,dlam,dnu)

set dual_base(Param p) = Param:
   let (dx,dlam,dnu) = dual_pieces(p)
   in parameter(dx,dlam,dnu)

{Original version, now not needed}
{ general p: the walk needs regular infinitesimal character, so translate first.
  The dual itself is unchanged by the translation, since dtf = gamma - lambda and
  dlambda depend on it only through quantities two_rho cancels out of. }
set dualQ (Param p) = Param:
(  let tworho = ratvec: p.root_datum.two_rho
   in dual_reg(parameter(p.x, p.lambda + tworho, p.nu + tworho))
)

set dual(Param p) = Param:
    let N = undual_hash.size()
    then n = undual_hash.match(p)
    in if n=N
       then dual_list#:= dual_base(p)
       fi;
       dual_list[n]

}

{ ------------------------------------- a row of Q, as one KL column on the dual }

{ Q[i][j] = P[sig[j]][sig[i]].  Fixing i at p makes the dual side the single KL
  column at dualQ(p), so only the downward closure of dualQ(p) is ever built.
  Returns that partial block and the column; Q_{p,q} is the entry at the index of
  dualQ(q) in it, and is zero for any q whose dual is absent. }
set Q_row (Param p) = ([Param],[vec]):
(  let (dB,M,polys) = partial_KL_block(dual(p))
   then n = #dB
in (dB, for e@t in dB do polys[M[n-1][t]] od)
)

{---------------------------}
{composition series using dualQ}

set pos_part(Split s) = int:
    let (a,b) = %s in abs(a+b)

set CSQ_time = int: 0

{this appears to work even if p is not final, although I'm not sure why}
{mult of irr q in std p <-> coeff of std pd in char of irr qd}
{low_diff_char(p,H) is a terrible way to decide whether to use this}
set composition_series_to_heightQ(Param p, int H) = ParamPol:
    let start = elapsed_ms(), Bp = partial_block(p), H0 = height(p)
    then () = if H<0 then H:=height(Bp[0]) fi
    then BpH_js = for q@j in Bp if q.height <= H do j fi od
    then BpH = for j in BpH_js do Bp[j] od, dp = dual(p)
    then dBpH = for q in BpH do dual(q) od {these qd are lower ht than pd}
    then dKLs = for dq in dBpH do KL_sum_at_s(dq) od
    then ans = sum(p.real_form, for dQ@i in dKLs do pos_part(dQ[dp])*BpH[i] od)
    in CSQ_time +:= elapsed_ms() - start; ans

set composition_series_to_heightQ(ParamPol P, int H) = ParamPol:
    map(((Param->ParamPol): (Param p): composition_series_to_heightQ(p, H)), P)

{i,j entry is mult of irr i in (partial block) in standard j; so always i <= j, mat is upper triang}
{column j is comp series of std #j <-> coeffs of std dj in irrs di}
set composition_series_mat_to_heightQ(Param p, int H) = mat:
    let Bp = partial_block(p) {block elts q of greater ht (closer to discrete series) than p;
    	     		      things that may occur}
    then () = if H < 0 then H:=height(Bp[0]) fi
    then BpH_js = for q@j in Bp do if q.height <= H then [j] else [] fi od.##
    then BpH = for j in BpH_js do Bp[j] od, pd = dual(p)
    then dBpH = for q in BpH do {regroup(pd.real_form,}dual(q){)} od {these qd are lower ht than pd}
    then dKLs = for dq in dBpH do KL_sum_at_s(dq) od
    then () = for dQi in dKLs do prints( dQi{for dqj in dBpH do pos_part(dQi[dqj]) od}) od {this is row i}
    then f(int i, int j) = pos_part(dKLs[i][dBpH[j]])
    in matrix((#dBpH,#dBpH),f)

set character_formula_to_heightQ(Param p, int H) = ParamPol:
   let Bp = partial_block(p) {block elts q of greater ht (closer to discrete series) than p;
    	     		      things that may occur}
   then () = if H < 0 then H:=height(Bp[0]) fi
   then BpH_js = for q@j in Bp if q.height <= H do j fi od
   then BpH = for j in BpH_js do Bp[j] od, dp = dual(p)
   then dBpH = for q in BpH do {regroup(dp.real_form,}dual(q){)} od {these dq are lower ht than dp}
   then dKLs = for dq in dBpH do KL_sum_at_s(dq) od {qd plus earlier q'd}
   then f(int i, int j) = pos_part(dKLs[i][dBpH[j]])
   then M = matrix((#dBpH,#dBpH),f), ppol = 1*p
   then pvec = vec: for q in BpH do int_part(ppol[q]) od {e(#BpH, #BpH-1)}
   then ansvec = solve(M,pvec).requisition
   in sum(p.real_form, for q@j in BpH do ansvec[j]*q od)

set character_formula_to_heightQ(ParamPol P, int H) = ParamPol:
    map(((Param->ParamPol): (Param p): character_formula_to_heightQ(p, H)), P)

{-----------------------------}

{ usage:
     ../atlasLTO   then   <dualQ.at
     set p = ...
     set d = dual(p)
     set (dB,col) = Q_row(p)
}
